      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© Journal of the Association of Physicians of India 2011.",
        "AbstractText": "Coronary cameral fistulae are rare and bicoronary pulmonary artery fistulae is even rarer. This is a case of a 70 year old male who presented to us with complaints of chest pain and dyspnoea. His ECG showed ST-T changes in inferior and anterior precordial leads suggestive of ischaemia in those territories. His coronary angiogram revealed bilateral coronary pulmonary arterial fistulae arising from left circumflex and right coronary artery and draining into pulmonary artery without any atherosclerotic narrowing of coronaries."
      },
